 "notes": "Look-test coords, core centre (5,5); add (11,11) for the game's 32x32 lattice (core centre (16,16)). The ring is a thin closed 8-connected curve: 28 cells, outer diameter 11, axis and diagonal steps alternating, so it reads as a circle in 2:1 iso. It seals the core because pathing is 4-connected (no diagonal steps), and because it is thin every single fence cell left as a gap or broken opens it (a 4-connected staircase ring would carry corner cells that open nothing). 6 wagons are permanent, unbreakable 2-cell wall pieces on the ring's orthogonal steps (roughly tangent; spacing 1-5 fence cells, irregular). Facing = the wagon's length in clockwise ring order: se/nw along +i/-i, sw/ne along +j/-j. 'gaps' lists the two cells the mock-up leaves open (they are among ring_fence_cells). interior_post_cells = every cell inside the ring except the 3x3 core.",
